                        "review": "TL:DR - A short read {~5 hrs} with limited choice based agency, this feels like a regression after more recent outings into Paradise Cove, but enjoyable none the less. \n\nThis game is more inline with the more classic paradise cove games, think Model Melissa, Water Girls, Negligee - all choice oriented semi-kinetic novels, and very unlike Maid-Cafe, which had significantly more agency than this outing.\n\nThe classic sprites are here, and a number of familiar faces from their earlier games in a new combination.  For the more animated scenes we can see some new animations, and new imagery coming into play.\n\nVery little on the kink side of things, i felt these could be more explored, but it's a relatively short novel, and some kinks kinda need enough time for them to be shown well, tho i was disappointed with Rei's events, the first week her character felt like it was going one way, the weekend hang out didn't really deliver on this, if anything, Stacey was more in line with where I'd've expected Rei\n\nOn the technical side of things, No game breaking bugs, {as you'd hope from veteran developers}  some immersion breaking issues, such as continuity bugs, and some text falling outside the text box, but nothing terrible.\n\nPersonally i'm hoping this is a filler, and not an indication of future games from this developer, i felt that Maid Cafe has been their peak so far, and sincerely hope that Burlesque is more like Maid Cafe than SwimMeet.",
